From: Balázs Triszka <info@balika011.hu>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2025 18:13:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: restore optional RTK SerDes patch

The Realtek SDK applies two additional host SerDes writes on platforms
which require the RTK SerDes tuning sequence. Support for selecting this
sequence was present in the original RTL826x driver conversion, but was
not retained when the driver was integrated for Linux 6.18.

Restore the board opt-in realtek,patch-rtk-serdes property and append the
two PSDS0 tuning operations after the common firmware patch table. Keep
the sequence opt-in because it is not valid for every RTL826x host.

Do not reset the DTE XS after applying the firmware table.
rtl826x_config_init() already performs the vendor 0x145 reset before
rtlgen_phy_patch(), matching the original driver order. A second reset at
the end of the table was found to clear firmware-programmed SDS 6.0x0d,
6.0x0e, and 6.0x1d bits. The PHY then reached Base-R block lock while the
AN7581 received no USXGMII partner word. Restoring those firmware values
and reapplying the two flow_s writes immediately raised AN_STATS_0 and
carrier on the affected XR1710G.

On the same board, the flow_s values change SDS 7.0x10 from 0x8003 to
0x80aa and SDS 6.0x12 from 0x00a4 to 0x5078. Repeated positive, negative,
and positive tests showed that these adjusted values eliminate the original
load-dependent retransmission stalls.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/commit/46d81ac28caf2e0018089da921e9ae953f6dd3d2
Signed-off-by: Balázs Triszka <info@balika011.hu>
[yyh: adapt the optional operations to the flex-array, little-endian patch database and preserve the vendor reset-before-patch ordering]
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/phy_patch_rtl826x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/phy_patch_rtl826x.c
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ static int rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init(str
 	struct rtlgen_phy_patch_db *patch_db;
 	struct rtlgen_hwpatch *patches;
 	const struct firmware *fw;
-	size_t count;
+	size_t count, extra_count, total_count;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = request_firmware_direct(&fw, fw_name, dev);
@@ -253,17 +253,43 @@ static int rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init(str
 
 	patches = (struct rtlgen_hwpatch *)fw->data;
 	count = fw->size / sizeof(*patches);
+	extra_count = priv->patch_rtk_serdes ? 2 : 0;
+	if (check_add_overflow(count, extra_count, &total_count)) {
+		ret = -EOVERFLOW;
+		goto out;
+	}
 
-	patch_db = devm_kzalloc(dev, struct_size(patch_db, conf, count), GFP_KERNEL);
+	patch_db = devm_kzalloc(dev, struct_size(patch_db, conf, total_count),
+				GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!patch_db) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	patch_db->count = count;
+	patch_db->count = total_count;
 	patch_db->patch_op_exec = rtl826x_phy_patch_op;
 
 	memcpy(patch_db->conf, patches, flex_array_size(patch_db, conf, count));
+	if (priv->patch_rtk_serdes) {
+		patch_db->conf[count] = (struct rtlgen_hwpatch) {
+			.patch_op = RTK_PATCH_OP_PSDS0,
+			.portmask = 0xff,
+			.pagemmd = cpu_to_le16(0x07),
+			.addr = cpu_to_le16(0x10),
+			.msb = 15,
+			.lsb = 0,
+			.data = cpu_to_le16(0x80aa),
+		};
+		patch_db->conf[count + 1] = (struct rtlgen_hwpatch) {
+			.patch_op = RTK_PATCH_OP_PSDS0,
+			.portmask = 0xff,
+			.pagemmd = cpu_to_le16(0x06),
+			.addr = cpu_to_le16(0x12),
+			.msb = 15,
+			.lsb = 0,
+			.data = cpu_to_le16(0x5078),
+		};
+	}
 
 	priv->patch = patch_db;
 
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 struct rtl826x_priv {
 	struct rtlgen_phy_patch_db *patch;
 	bool enable_pma_low_power:1;
+	bool patch_rtk_serdes:1;
 };
 
 int rtl822x_hwmon_init(struct phy_device *phydev);
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2378,6 +2378,8 @@ static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_devi
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	priv->enable_pma_low_power = device_property_read_bool(dev, "realtek,enable-pma-low-power");
+	priv->patch_rtk_serdes =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "realtek,patch-rtk-serdes");
 	phydev->priv = priv;
 
 	if (!priv->enable_pma_low_power)
